  "title": "Zenobia",
  "summary": "Zenobia was queen of Palmyra, a prosperous city in the Roman East (modern Tadmor, Syria). After her husband Odaenathus died in 267 she served as regent for their son and then expanded her authority and territory. In 272 the emperor Aurelian made war on the Palmyrenes; accounts say she was captured fleeing toward the Euphrates, and her later fate is unclear.",
